DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       This program is part of NNeettppbbmm(1).

       ppggmmnnooiissee creates a PGM image that  is  made  up  of  pixels  of  random
       brightness.

       You specify the dimensions of the image with the _w_i_d_t_h and _h_e_i_g_h_t argu‐
       ments.

       The randomness in the image is limited before  Netpbm  10.37  (December
       2006)  --  if you run the program twice in the same second, you may get
       identical output.



OOPPTTIIOONNSS
       In addition to the options common to all programs  based  on  libnetpbm
       (most notably --qquuiieett, see
        Common  Options  ⟨index.html#commonoptions⟩ ), ppggmmnnooiissee recognizes the
       following command line options:



       --mmaaxxvvaall==_n
              The maxval of the generated image.

              Default is 255.

              This option was new in Netpbm 10.63 (June 2013).


       --rraannddoommsseeeedd==_i_n_t_e_g_e_r
              This is the seed for the random number generator that  generates
              the pixels.

              Use  this  to  ensure you get the same image on separate invoca‐
              tions.

              By default, ppggmmnnooiissee uses a seed derived from the  time  of  day
              and  process  ID, which gives you fairly uncorrelated results in
              multiple invocations.

              This option was new in Netpbm 10.45 (December 2008).




